  "summary": "Re-census of all 54 corpus rows under the ORACLE POLICY CHANGE (annex C, commit 4e6694d): kernel certificates are the certification, recorded OCC references are diagnostics, the 1e-4 band is retired as a gate. Fresh python per row, serial, quiet machine, release-built truck123d at HEAD f827556 (built once), door_version 2. GREEN predicate = kernel constructs + volume certificate bracket present + solid_count constructive + bbox carrier-derived + mesh emits. Result: 11 green / 30 typed-refusal / 13 DNF. The 11 green rows are the full constructible Falcon-Heavy canonical subset (nozzle, chamber, thrust_structure, turbopump, gas_generator, turbine_exhaust, feed, harness, engine_prototype, mvac, fairing), each with an exact bracket (lo==hi) and the kernel timing series in docs/TT_TIMING_RESULTS.md. Four green rows carry OCC volume deltas beyond the retired 1e-4 band (feed -1.65e-2, gas_generator -6.55e-3, turbine_exhaust -4.05e-3, harness -1.79e-3) and two carry a recorded OCC volume of 0 (engine_prototype, mvac); the deltas are reported, never compared. No F1 row is green: 21 enrolled F1 rows (15 typed-refusal, 6 DNF) plus the six staged rows (5 typed-refusal, 1 DNF). The policy moved no F1 row; it closed the FH canonical subset. The four corner rows moved from untyped DNF to typed refusal (MONO-1 data rows). V5 net holds: the three previously-green FH timing rows are bit-identical. The six staged rows (front_wing, cockpit, nose, sidepod_left, sidepod_right, halo) were enrolled in MANIFEST.json + SKIPS.json (the packet's stated 54-row scope and anchor A1), and their OCC reference recordings were staged as diagnostics (sidepods exceed the recording bound -> absent-diagnostic).",
